{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #397: declared status 'disproved'. Formalized: yes. Are there only finitely many solutions to\\[\\prod_i \\binom{2m_i}{m_i}=\\prod_j \\binom{2n_j}{n_j}\\]with the $m_i,n_j$ distinct? Current best: In fact, for any $a\\geq 2$, if $c=8a^2+8a+1$,\\[\\binom{2a}{a}\\binom{4a+4}{2a+2}\\binom{2c}{c}= \\binom{2a+2}{a+1}\\binom{4a}{2a}\\binom{2c+2}{c+1}.\\]Further families of solutions are given in the comments by SharkyKesa. Prize: no. Tags: binomial coefficients, number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_e00608ce263e6b56af370707f102b3fdebb1663179af25a06a4582e33028d5bc","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:397","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_c6eae709ccb1b19c","object_root":"sha256:4dd55d53ad372984a27ea043b5f59271e452a0fd4f42bd674fd2d8d1a0d9c4ac","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:397"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}